<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title></title><link>https://www.futilitycloset.com/</link><description>闲人的简明娱乐杂项</description><lastBuildDate>Fri, 08 May 2026 08:00:32 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>文字与音乐</title><link>https://www.futilitycloset.com/2026/11/24/words-and-music-5/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;这很有趣——1904 年，&lt;em&gt;斯特兰德&lt;/em&gt;派了一位音乐家到议会，用乐谱记录演讲者声音的音高和节奏。一些例子： &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="https://archive.org/details/the-strand/The%20Strand%20v27%201904/page/140/mode/2up" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-74775" height="299" src="https://www.futilitycloset.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-11-24-words-and-music-buxton.png" width="737" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;西德尼·巴克斯顿（Sydney Buxton）“经常简短地讲话，但他可以在很短的时间内塞满大量单词，是众议院中发言速度最快的人之一。主要音调是升 C 音，转调很少有变化，演讲被分解成简短的短语，每个短语末尾都有向下的音调。” &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="https://archive.org/details/the-strand/The%20Strand%20v27%201904/page/140/mode/2up" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-74776" height="295" src="https://www.futilitycloset.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-11-24-words-and-music-fenwick.png" width="739" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;查尔斯·芬威克（Charles Fenwick）“可能声称自己是最低调的。他强烈、充满活力、响亮的风格很好地体现了他的性格，正是这种性格将其主人从煤矿工作提升到了议会席位。” &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="https://archive.org/details/the-strand/The%20Strand%20v27%201904/page/140/mode/2up" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-74778" height="315" src="https://www.futilitycloset.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-11-24-words-and-music-lloyd-george.png" width="757" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;大卫·劳埃德·乔治“拥有灵活、轻盈、清晰、令人愉悦的声音。……当心情实用时，他在 D 和 E 上相处得很好，但在其他时候，他会跨越相当大的间隔。” &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="https://archive.org/details/the-strand/The%20Strand%20v27%201904/page/140/mode/2up" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-74779" height="447" src="https://www.futilitycloset.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-11-24-words-and-music-balfour.png" width="753" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;首相阿瑟·贝尔福的声音“在音色上有一种难以定义的东西，就像人们在一流男中音的歌唱中所听到的那样……他说话最多的音调介于 D 和 E 之间，但他经常在 G 到 G 之间调整八度音阶。”&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; &lt;a href="https://archive.org/details/the-strand/The%20Strand%20v27%201904/page/140/mode/2up"&gt;The whole article is here.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class="entry-meta"&gt; &lt;span class="posted-on"&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.futilitycloset.com/2026/11/24/words-and-music-5/" rel="bookmark"&gt;&lt;time class="entry-date published" datetime="2026-11-24T02:33:41-04:00"&gt;November 24, 2026&lt;/time&gt; &lt;time class="updated" datetime="2026-11-23T12:41:12-04:00"&gt;November 23, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="cat-links"&gt;|&lt;a href="https://www.futilitycloset.com/category/history/" rel="category tag"&gt;历史&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 10:15:30 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.futilitycloset.com/2026/11/24/words-and-music-5/</guid></item><item><title>句法</title><link>https://www.futilitycloset.com/2026/11/23/syntax/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="https://archive.org/details/portfolioselecti00lond/page/74/mode/2up" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-74763" height="400" src="https://www.futilitycloset.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-11-23-syntax.jpg" width="359" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;摘自&lt;a href="https://archive.org/details/portfolioselecti00lond/page/74/mode/2up"&gt;&lt;em&gt;《投资组合》&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt; ，1820 年。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class="entry-meta"&gt; &lt;span class="posted-on"&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.futilitycloset.com/2026/11/23/syntax/" rel="bookmark"&gt;&lt;time class="entry-date published" datetime="2026-11-23T14:08:30-04:00"&gt;十一月 23, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;time class="updated" datetime="2026-11-22T21:12:46-04:00"&gt;十一月 22, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="cat-links"&gt;|&lt;a href="https://www.futilitycloset.com/category/language/" rel="category tag"&gt;语言&lt;/a&gt;·&lt;a href="https://www.futilitycloset.com/category/uncategorized/" rel="category tag"&gt;未分类&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 21:44:10 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.futilitycloset.com/2026/11/23/syntax/</guid></item><item><title>索迪的六边形</title><link>https://www.futilitycloset.com/2026/11/23/soddys-hexlet/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Illustration-hexlet2.gif" src="https://www.futilitycloset.com/2026-11-23-soddys-hexlet.gif" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; Set two spheres against one another and wrap them in a third, as shown. Now add a new sphere, tangent to the first two and to the large enclosing sphere. Surprisingly, if you keep adding these new spheres, tangent to one another, they&amp;#39;ll always form a “necklace” of six.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; English radiochemist Frederick Soddy discovered this pretty fact in 1937, though it had been known to Japanese mathematicians since at least 1822. Soddy, who had written &lt;a href="https://www.futilitycloset.com/2014/06/19/descartes-theorem/"&gt;a paean to Descartes&amp;#39; theorem&lt;/a&gt; in &lt;em&gt;Nature&lt;/em&gt; in June 1936, added another that December to celebrate his finding:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; However ill-assorted in girth three spheres may be&lt;br /&gt;每个人可以同时亲吻另外两个&lt;br /&gt;一个六人环，他们都在连续接吻。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;尽管任何分级珠子的项链&lt;br /&gt;可能适合一般的女性，&lt;br /&gt;我的这个设计新颖的六边形&lt;br /&gt;抚摸的不是一个而是三个脖子。&lt;br /&gt;然而它的磨损会改变它的等级&lt;br /&gt;为了适应它的三球形监狱，&lt;br /&gt;玩环圈接吻和旋转木马&lt;br /&gt;同时精准地抱住三个脖子。&lt;br /&gt;就像泡沫一样，吹起、点燃、消失&lt;br /&gt;它经得起轻松的嘲笑&lt;br /&gt;纯抑扬符的构成&lt;br /&gt;以及它对精神倒错的厌恶&lt;br /&gt;那将有“It&amp;#39;s 1/ &lt;em&gt;x&lt;/em&gt; ”。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;历代圣贤&lt;br /&gt;从未偏离过一种信念，&lt;br /&gt;紧紧抓住变化中不变的东西&lt;br /&gt;并找出保存下来的东西。&lt;br /&gt;现在这些毫无瑕疵的珠子遵守第一定律&lt;br /&gt;为它们弯曲的总和。&lt;br /&gt;当隧道中的每个人都通过漏斗变细时&lt;br /&gt;它的&lt;em&gt;相对&lt;/em&gt;严重膨胀。&lt;br /&gt;&lt;em&gt;但是每对相对的弯曲的平均值&lt;br /&gt;是三者之总和。&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class="entry-meta"&gt; &lt;span class="posted-on"&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.futilitycloset.com/2026/11/23/soddys-hexlet/" rel="bookmark"&gt;&lt;time class="entry-date published" datetime="2026-11-23T02:37:36-04:00"&gt;十一月 23, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;time class="updated" datetime="2026-11-22T16:28:00-04:00"&gt;十一月 22, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="cat-links"&gt;|&lt;a href="https://www.futilitycloset.com/category/science-math/" rel="category tag"&gt;科学与数学&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 10:05:32 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.futilitycloset.com/2026/11/23/soddys-hexlet/</guid></item><item><title>一小步</title><link>https://www.futilitycloset.com/2026/11/22/one-small-step/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="https://archive.org/details/lifesurprisingad00defo/page/146/mode/2up" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-74738" height="682" src="https://www.futilitycloset.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-11-22-one-small-step-1.jpg" width="700" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;星期五是如何留下一个足迹让鲁滨逊漂流记发现的呢？&lt;/p&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;我上岸，又下岸，但都是一体的；除了那个印象之外，我看不到其他印象。我又去看了一遍，看看是否还有更多，看看这是否是我的幻觉。 but there was no room for that, for there was exactly the very print of a foot — toes, heel, and every part of a foot. How it came thither I knew not, nor could in the least imagine.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt; “那个脚印是某个可怕的跳跃食人者留下的吗？”约翰·萨瑟兰 (John Sutherland) 在&lt;a href="https://archive.org/details/foliobookofliter0000john/page/98/mode/2up"&gt;&lt;em&gt;《文学谜题对开本》(The Folio Book of Literary Puzzles&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt; )（2007 年）中问道。 “也许长约翰·西尔弗从&lt;em&gt;金银岛&lt;/em&gt;路过，只有一只脚和一条假腿？有人对鲁滨逊漂流记做过恶作剧，像在跳远坑里那样在沙子上耙地，只留下一个不祥的痕迹吗？”&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; （严格来说，星期五直到本集七年后才出现，所以可能他没有留下印刷品。但有人留下了！）&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class="entry-meta"&gt; &lt;span class="posted-on"&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.futilitycloset.com/2026/11/22/one-small-step/" rel="bookmark"&gt;&lt;time class="entry-date published" datetime="2026-11-22T02:21:44-04:00"&gt;十一月 22, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;time class="updated" datetime="2026-11-21T14:31:40-04:00"&gt;十一月 21, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="cat-links"&gt;|&lt;a href="https://www.futilitycloset.com/category/literature/" rel="category tag"&gt;文学&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 11:00:46 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.futilitycloset.com/2026/11/22/one-small-step/</guid></item><item><title></title><link>https://www.futilitycloset.com/2026/11/21/stick-figures/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;Move one matchstick to make this equation valid: &lt;/p&gt;&lt;figure class="wp-caption aligncenter" id="attachment_74729" style="width: 600px;"&gt;&lt;img alt="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Matchstick_puzzle_and_solution.png" class="size-full wp-image-74729" height="234" src="https://www.futilitycloset.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-11-21-stick-figures-1.png" width="600" /&gt;&lt;figcaption class="wp-caption-text" id="caption-attachment-74729"&gt;图片：&lt;a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Matchstick_puzzle_and_solution.png"&gt;维基共享资源&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;div class="easySpoilerWrapper"&gt;&lt;table align="center" bgcolor="FFFFFF" border="0" class="easySpoilerTable" style="text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr style="white-space: normal;"&gt;&lt;th class="easySpoilerTitleA" style="white-space: normal; font-weight: normal; text-align: left; vertical-align: middle; font-size: 120%;"&gt;&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th class="easySpoilerTitleB" style="text-align: right; vertical-align: middle; font-size: 100%; white-space: nowrap;"&gt; &lt;a align="right" class="easySpoilerButtonOther" href="https://rssweball.top/feed/ccbb3564-2d59-4685-b89e-ffe9047f2ba5.xml" style="font-size: 100%; background-color: #fcfcfc; background-image: none; border-style: solid; border-color: #cccccc; display: none; margin: 3px 0px 3px; padding: 4px;"&gt;选择&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a align="right" class="easySpoilerButton" href="https://rssweball.top/feed/ccbb3564-2d59-4685-b89e-ffe9047f2ba5.xml" id="spoilerDiv76ae8001_action" style="font-size: 100%; background-color: #fcfcfc; background-image: none; border-style: solid; border-color: #cccccc; margin: 3px 0px 3px 5px; padding: 4px;" value="Click for Answer"&gt;点击回答&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="easySpoilerRow" colspan="2"&gt;&lt;div class="easySpoilerSpoils" id="spoilerDiv76ae8001" style="display: none; white-space: wrap; overflow: auto; vertical-align: middle;"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;figure class="wp-caption aligncenter" id="attachment_74730" style="width: 600px;"&gt;&lt;img alt="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Matchstick_puzzle_and_solution.png" class="size-full wp-image-74730" height="229" src="https://www.futilitycloset.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-11-21-stick-figures-2.png" width="600" /&gt;&lt;figcaption class="wp-caption-text" id="caption-attachment-74730"&gt;图片：&lt;a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Matchstick_puzzle_and_solution.png"&gt;维基共享资源&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;div class="easySpoilerConclude"&gt;&lt;table align="center" bgcolor="FFFFFF" border="0" class="easySpoilerTable" frame="box" style="text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th class="easySpoilerEnd" style="width: 100%;"&gt;&lt;/th&gt;&lt;td class="easySpoilerEnd" colspan="2" style="white-space: nowrap;"&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="easySpoilerGroupWrapperLastRow" colspan="2"&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="entry-meta"&gt; &lt;span class="posted-on"&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.futilitycloset.com/2026/11/21/stick-figures/" rel="bookmark"&gt;&lt;time class="entry-date published" datetime="2026-11-21T02:48:36-04:00"&gt;November 21, 2026&lt;/time&gt; &lt;time class="updated" datetime="2026-11-20T20:50:36-04:00"&gt;November 20, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="cat-links"&gt;|&lt;a href="https://www.futilitycloset.com/category/puzzles/" rel="category tag"&gt;谜题&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:25:11 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.futilitycloset.com/2026/11/21/stick-figures/</guid></item><item><title>首要地位</title><link>https://www.futilitycloset.com/2026/11/20/primacy/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Desembarco_de_Col%C3%B3n_de_Di%C3%B3scoro_Puebla.jpg" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-74720" height="605" src="https://www.futilitycloset.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-11-20-primacy.jpg" width="1000" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;伟大的发现者不一定是伟人。谁比哥伦布更能改变世界？他是什么？一个冒险家。他确实有性格，但他并不是一个伟人。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt; ——弗洛伊德，欧内斯特·琼斯在&lt;em&gt;《西格蒙德·弗洛伊德的生活与工作》&lt;/em&gt;中引用，1953-57&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class="entry-meta"&gt;&lt;span class="posted-on"&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.futilitycloset.com/2026/11/20/primacy/" rel="bookmark"&gt;&lt;time class="entry-date published" datetime="2026-11-20T14:26:56-04:00"&gt;十一月 20, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;time class="updated" datetime="2026-11-19T19:28:14-04:00"&gt;十一月 19, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="cat-links"&gt;|&lt;a href="https://www.futilitycloset.com/category/history/" rel="category tag"&gt;历史&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 22:04:21 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.futilitycloset.com/2026/11/20/primacy/</guid></item><item><title>抽查</title><link>https://www.futilitycloset.com/2026/11/20/spot-check/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;英国经济学家威廉·斯坦利·杰文斯 (William Stanley Jevons) 于 1875 年发表了一篇引人注目的论文： &lt;a href="https://archive.org/details/in.ernet.dli.2015.228276/page/n225/mode/2up"&gt;《论太阳黑子周期对玉米价格的影响》。&lt;/a&gt;他说他的统计研究表明商业周期随太阳黑子活动而变化：&lt;/p&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;任何一年的收成是否成功当然取决于天气，尤其是夏季和秋季的天气。现在，如果这种天气在某种程度上取决于太阳周期，那么谷物的收成和价格将或多或少地取决于太阳周期，并且将在与太阳黑子相同的时间周期内经历周期性波动。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;这个想法并未得到证实，但 2001 年的一项研究发现&lt;a href="https://scholarsarchive.byu.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=10180&amp;amp;context=facpub"&gt;，晴朗的天气对股票收益的影响很小&lt;/a&gt;——可能是因为它改善了交易者的情绪。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class="entry-meta"&gt; &lt;span class="posted-on"&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.futilitycloset.com/2026/11/20/spot-check/" rel="bookmark"&gt;&lt;time class="entry-date published" datetime="2026-11-20T02:03:56-04:00"&gt;十一月 20, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;time class="updated" datetime="2026-11-20T03:31:59-04:00"&gt;十一月 20, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="cat-links"&gt;|&lt;a href="https://www.futilitycloset.com/category/oddities/" rel="category tag"&gt;怪事&lt;/a&gt;·&lt;a href="https://www.futilitycloset.com/category/science-math/" rel="category tag"&gt;科学与数学&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 10:32:45 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.futilitycloset.com/2026/11/20/spot-check/</guid></item><item><title></title><link>https://www.futilitycloset.com/2026/11/19/insinuation/</link><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;There is much that he does not say that he means, that he knows you know he means, and so you cannot contradict what he does not say, what you know he means to say — and yet you cannot agree with what he does say, for you know that that will be taken to mean that you agree with what he does not say as well, and to the latter you are firmly opposed.我希望读者能够度过这一难关。这就是我读完《X》后的感受。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt; — From an &lt;a href="https://archive.org/details/sim_mathematical-gazette_1916-07_8_124/page/298/mode/2up"&gt;unpublished review&lt;/a&gt; in the &lt;em&gt;Mathematical Gazette&lt;/em&gt; , July 1916&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class="entry-meta"&gt; &lt;span class="posted-on"&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.futilitycloset.com/2026/11/19/insinuation/" rel="bookmark"&gt;&lt;time class="entry-date published" datetime="2026-11-19T14:00:55-04:00"&gt;十一月 19, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;time class="updated" datetime="2026-11-18T21:09:34-04:00"&gt;十一月 18, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="cat-links"&gt;|&lt;a href="https://www.futilitycloset.com/category/society/" rel="category tag"&gt;社会&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 21:36:47 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.futilitycloset.com/2026/11/19/insinuation/</guid></item><item><title>第一个朋友</title><link>https://www.futilitycloset.com/2026/11/18/the-first-friend/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Illustration_(b)_at_p._223_in_Just_So_Stories_(c1912).png" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-74703" height="291" src="https://www.futilitycloset.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2026-11-18-the-first-friend.png" width="800" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;野狗到了洞口，用鼻子掀起干马皮，闻着烤羊肉的香味，女人看着刀骨，听了他的话，笑道：“第一个来了。” Wild Thing out of the Wild Woods, what do you want?&amp;#39;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; Wild Dog said, &amp;#39;O my Enemy and Wife of my Enemy, what is this that smells so good in the Wild Woods?&amp;#39;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; Then the Woman picked up a roasted mutton-bone and threw it to Wild Dog, and said, &amp;#39;Wild Thing out of the Wild Woods, taste and try.&amp;#39;野狗咬了骨头，它比他尝过的任何东西都好吃，他说：“哦，我的敌人和我敌人的妻子，再给我一根吧。”&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;女人说道：“野林里的野物，帮我的男人白天打猎，晚上看守这个山洞，你需要多少烤骨头，我就给你多少。”&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; &amp;#39;啊！&amp;#39;猫边听边说道。 &amp;#39;This is a very wise Woman, but she is not so wise as I am.&amp;#39;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;野狗爬进山洞，把头放在女人的腿上，说道：“哦，我的朋友和我朋友的妻子，我将帮助你的男人白天打猎，晚上我将守卫你的山洞。”&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; &amp;#39;啊！&amp;#39;猫边听边说道。 “那是一只非常愚蠢的狗。” And he went back through the Wet Wild Woods waving his wild tail, and walking by his wild lone.但他从未告诉过任何人。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; When the Man waked up he said, &amp;#39;What is Wild Dog doing here?&amp;#39; And the Woman said, &amp;#39;His name is not Wild Dog any more, but the First Friend, because he will be our friend for always and always and always.你去打猎的时候带上他。”&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt; — Kipling, “The Cat That Walked by Himself,” from &lt;a href="https://www.google.com/books/edition/The_Writings_in_Prose_and_Verse_of_Rudya/KO8tAAAAYAAJ?hl=en&amp;amp;gbpv=1&amp;amp;pg=PA205&amp;amp;printsec=frontcover"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Just So Stories&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt; , 1902&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class="entry-meta"&gt; &lt;span class="posted-on"&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.futilitycloset.com/2026/11/18/the-first-friend/" rel="bookmark"&gt;&lt;time class="entry-date published" datetime="2026-11-18T14:30:19-04:00"&gt;十一月 18, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;time class="updated" datetime="2026-11-17T20:31:57-04:00"&gt;十一月 17, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="cat-links"&gt;|&lt;a href="https://www.futilitycloset.com/category/literature/" rel="category tag"&gt;文学&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 21:54:52 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.futilitycloset.com/2026/11/18/the-first-friend/</guid></item><item><title></title><link>https://www.futilitycloset.com/2026/11/18/as-indicated/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;From &lt;a href="https://x.com/MerriamWebster"&gt;Merriam-Webster&amp;#39;s Twitter feed&lt;/a&gt; :&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; Vitamin C is also called ascorbic acid.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;源自希腊语的前缀&lt;em&gt;a-&lt;/em&gt;意思是“不，没有”。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; &lt;em&gt;Scorbutus&lt;/em&gt; in New Latin means “scurvy.”&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; So ascorbic acid is “no-scurvy acid.”&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; （谢谢，莎伦。）&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class="entry-meta"&gt; &lt;span class="posted-on"&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.futilitycloset.com/2026/11/18/as-indicated/" rel="bookmark"&gt;&lt;time class="entry-date published" datetime="2026-11-18T02:54:10-04:00"&gt;十一月 18, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;time class="updated" datetime="2026-11-17T19:54:37-04:00"&gt;十一月 17, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="cat-links"&gt;|&lt;a href="https://www.futilitycloset.com/category/language/" rel="category tag"&gt;语言&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 10:19:36 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.futilitycloset.com/2026/11/18/as-indicated/</guid></item></channel></rss>